  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday morning through next Monday)\nIssued at 248 PM EDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nBy Wed night the cold front that moved into the area in the short \nterm will still be moving south through the state moving into South \nGA/N FL by Thu morning. This boundary stalls near the FL/GA border \nbut it does usher in some drier air which should keep North and \nCentral GA precipitation free through Friday night. Temps are not \nexpected to cool to much Thu/Fri with high temps still expected in \nthe upper 80s to middle 90s but the Apparent T (feels like temps) \nwill be much lower.\n\nBy Sat the next frontal boundary moving east out of the lower to mid \nMS river valley moves into W GA just before daybreak. The main low \npressure center moves east into western KY at the same time. With \nthe close proximity of the low center to NW GA this frontal boundary \nshould stay fairly organized as it moves into the region. The \ncurrent forecast models show this front stalling across E/SE GA and \nthe Carolinas through Tues keeping the area in  moist S to SW flow \nthrough day 7. This will keep precip chances elevated through day\n7.",
